<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b802ef94-e1b5-5555-8232-bf304276c96f" activityNameId="036e4921-f05e-5f88-b98c-349f90523c1f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Transport, aircraft, passenger, medium-haul, business</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Transport, aircraft, passenger, medium-haul, business
Inventory refers to the entire transport life cycle. Airport infrastructure expenditures and environmental interventions are accounted for using the yearly transport performance at Zurich airport (73'526'350'051 pkm/a). Aircraft manufacturing is allocated based on the total life span of an aircraft (50'000 LTO), the average distance of a flight (2800km) and allocated according to the area of a seat in the economy class  and its transport performance of economy passenger (110p/unit);
UUID: f858d9f9-ba49-3204-8fc7-2f7c6f2af300
The dataset describes the operation of aircrafts including taxying, take-off and landing covering fuel consumption and operation emissions. Aircraft manufacture and maintenance, airport construction, operation and dismantling are inputs to this dataset
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Aircraft operation modelled based on passenger aircrafts operated by Lufthansa Group in 2019. The emission profiles distinguish between LTO and cruise.
Time period: Start date refers to emission factor data. End date refers to year of reporting fuel consumption and transport activities
Production volume: 33'060'000'000pkm
Sampling: fuel consumption is based on corporate data, emission profiles are based on FOEN statistics 
Extrapolations: Allocation between passengers and freight based on weight (average passenger weight between 158kg and 163kg); allocation between booking classes based on seat area.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f858d9f9-ba49-3204-8fc7-2f7c6f2af300.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">RER</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location: &lt;null&gt;</text>
        </comment>
      </geography>
      <technology>
        <comment>
